course: dictionary
lesson: 4372
title: Gymnastics: a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gymnastics is a sport. You do it on mats and on beams and bars, and it shows strength, balance and flexibility. Rolls, cartwheels and handstands are all gymnastics.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Mental gymnastics» has nothing to do with the body. It means very clever or difficult thinking, like working out a hard puzzle in your head.
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. The sentence «Gymnastics needs a warm-up, mats and a coach» is about the sport. Swap in your meaning, a sport of exercises, and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Safety comes first. The sentences show that experts learn with a coach, warm-ups and thick mats, because a flip tried alone can cause a serious injury.
fact: Gymnastics is a noun, and the adjective is gymnastic.
fact: «Gymnastics» means a sport of exercises that show strength, balance and flexibility.
fact: «Mental gymnastics» means very clever or difficult thinking.
fact: A forward roll lands on the back of the shoulders with the chin tucked, never on the top of the head.
fact: Flips are learned over months with a coach, spotters and thick mats.
exercise: «Gymnastics needs a warm-up, mats and a coach who teaches the moves.» What does gymnastics mean here? | A kind of dance on ice | A sort of race on a track | A type of clever thinking | *A sport of exercises like rolls and handstands
exercise: Dad says, «Doing that crossword is pure mental gymnastics!» What does he mean? | *The crossword needs very clever, difficult thinking | He is doing a handstand | He is very tired from running | He is doing a sport on the mat
exercise: «Flips are learned over months with a coach, spotters and thick mats.» Find and copy the word that tells you how long learning flips takes. | spotters | thick | *months | mats
test: «Gymnastics is about control.» According to this sentence, what is gymnastics about? | *Control of your body and your moves | Speed in running races | Singing loudly in a choir | Eating healthy food
test: Why should you learn a flip with a coach and thick mats? | *To stay safe, because a flip tried alone can cause a serious injury | It is not important at all | Because mats are soft to sit on | To make the flip faster
exam: What is the best way to check the meaning of a word in a sentence? | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Look only at the first letter of the word | Ignore the sentence and read only the title | Guess and never check
